<p class="prose">Slide 27 draws eight structures under &ldquo;Drug FGs&rdquo; and prints no labels; he named them in lecture: imidazoline, sulfone, sulfonamide, then, below, ester, carbamate, steroid, prostaglandins, and aryloxypropanolamine (T@37388 to T@38473 11/18). The first eight rows follow those drawings. Exam cue: the question could simply ask what chemical class a drug belongs to (T@38473 11/18).</p>
