<tr><td><b>2. Beta blockers</b></td><td>Decrease aqueous humor production</td><td>20&ndash;30%</td><td><span class="ln">Timolol 0.25%, 0.5% (Timoptic, Istalol); gel Timoptic-XE</span><span class="ln">Betaxolol (Betoptic 0.5%, Betoptic-S 0.25%)</span><span class="ln">Carteolol 1% (Ocupress)</span><span class="ln">Levobunolol 0.25%, 0.5% (Betagan)</span><span class="ln">Combination: Cosopt, Cosopt PF, Combigan</span></td><td>BID; Timoptic-XE once daily</td><td><span class="ln">Stinging on application (especially betaxolol solution)</span><span class="ln">Dry eyes</span><span class="ln">Blepharitis</span><span class="ln">Blurred vision</span></td><td><span class="ln">Bradycardia</span><span class="ln">Hypotension</span><span class="ln">Bronchospasm</span></td><td><span class="ln">Asthma/COPD</span><span class="ln">Bradycardia, second or third degree heart block</span><span class="ln">Uncompensated cardiac failure</span><span class="ln">Oral beta-blocker therapy</span><span class="ln">(less risk with betaxolol and carteolol)</span></td><td>Lam Glaucoma slide 31, 32, 33, 34</td></tr>
